    journalctl - A journal where computer stores its activities and events, i.e, Logging System
                 It makes retrieving and viewing logfiles much easier.
                 Typing journalctl on screen shows every log entry on you sceen that can be useful
                 but has to much information so we can use different flags/options with journalctl
                 to make the work easier
                
                Log Priorities: Reflect different priorities for the operating system and sysadmin
                List: emerg(0), alert(1), crit(2), err(3), warning(4), notice(5), info(6), debug(7)
                command: journalctl -p "prority/priority-number"
                         journalctl -u service # To view log of a particular entry
